\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces $\varphi $-stratified completion vs.\ broadcast cadence $K$ (dedicated peer sweep: scarcity cells, random layouts, 20 seeds, episode-cluster bootstrap CIs). As $K$ shrinks, the warp share $P(W^{\star }|M^{\star })$ grows from $0.11$ to $0.55$ while $P(C^{\star }|W^{\star })$ stays below $0.05$ and the own-stratum rate stays flat: the completion collapse of fast sharing is concentrated in the $W^{\star }$ stratum, giving the Q/R/M/C bottleneck shift reported in the companion Q/R/M/C evaluation study \citep  {songlines1} its mechanistic reading. The share uptick at $K{=}16$ (broadcasts are rare, but agents also discover little on their own) is reported as observed.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{p2:fig:strata}{{1}{4}{$\varphi $-stratified completion vs.\ broadcast cadence $K$ (dedicated peer sweep: scarcity cells, random layouts, 20 seeds, episode-cluster bootstrap CIs). As $K$ shrinks, the warp share $P(\wstar |\mstar )$ grows from $0.11$ to $0.55$ while $P(\cstar |\wstar )$ stays below $0.05$ and the own-stratum rate stays flat: the completion collapse of fast sharing is concentrated in the $\wstar $ stratum, giving the Q/R/M/C bottleneck shift reported in the companion Q/R/M/C evaluation study \citep {songlines1} its mechanistic reading. The share uptick at $K{=}16$ (broadcasts are rare, but agents also discover little on their own) is reported as observed}{figure.1}{}}
